Pi Tech Lab / ScholarPi: two licenses

Copyright (c) 2026 Ali Vafadar Yengejeh (Pi Tech Lab).

This repository holds two kinds of work, under two licenses.

1. The science engines: open source, under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only
   (LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt; SPDX: AGPL-3.0-only). Anyone may use, study, change and share them. Anyone who
   runs a changed version for users over a network must offer those users the source of their version (AGPL
   section 13).

     backend/rubric.py          the Pi-Index scoring rubric
     backend/brain.py           the assessment pipeline: the AI panel, the judge, the scoring
     backend/providers.py       routing to the panel's models
     backend/scientometrics.py  interdisciplinarity, reference integrity, authorship-assistance signal
     backend/attribution.py     who a manuscript's credit belongs to
     backend/security.py        prompt-injection and manipulation checks
     backend/extraction.py      bibliographic extraction
     backend/integrations.py    bibliographic lookups (OpenAlex, Crossref)
     backend/http_client.py     the shared outbound HTTP client they use
     backend/diagnostics.py     reception diagnostics
     backend/ledger.py          the proof-of-research ledger's hashing and records
     rust/numbers/              the constants (pi, e, phi, gamma) in Rust, and frontend/numbers.wasm built from it

   Each of these files carries an SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only header.
   Note: brain.py and ledger.py also import platform modules that stay proprietary (for example the database,
   configuration, piQ emission and siM). The open files are licensed as listed; those modules are not.

2. Everything else, including the website and its design: proprietary, all rights reserved
   (LICENSES/LicenseRef-PiTechLab-Proprietary.txt). That is the front end and its look, the superellipse and
   glass interface, the SuperAI language and its engines (rust/superai, rust/pifront, frontend/super/), the
   site's program, and the platform that runs the service.

3. Third-party work keeps its own license, beside it:
     frontend/vendor/three/          three.js, MIT
     frontend/hal/vendor/v86/        v86 (BSD-2-Clause) and SeaBIOS (LGPL-3.0)
     frontend/quvi/                  QuVI, MIT (see LICENSE-QuVI.txt)
     frontend/fonts/                 Geist and Geist Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1
   The JavaScript libraries loaded from cdnjs (Chart.js, Mermaid, anime.js) are under their own licenses.

Before 13 October 2026 the repository had no license at its root (all rights reserved), and rust/numbers,
rust/superai and rust/pifront declared MIT in their Cargo.toml; copies obtained under those declarations keep
the rights MIT gave them.
